 "decisions": [
  "El Vigia's chain is 14 plinths authored here (24 to 40 studs apart, bible section 4); the chain crosses the trail twice, so the contest is fought on the trail.",
  "Occluder boxes come straight from the kit report (columns 3.9 x 4.6 x 11, wall 14.3 x 3 x 7, piers 6.4 x 6.8 x 11) and are recorded per instance with the measured base height; the shortest is 7 studs, above a standing avatar.",
  "Eight reliquaries sit in three-wall alcoves (24 walls) that open toward the trail, with a clear access lane; each alcove must be visible from at most two plinths. The other 16 walls are screens that face the nearest plinth, so a player can break line of sight on purpose.",
  "Stair runs are paired back to back as four overlook ridges 23.5 studs beside the trail; the bible gives stairs no purpose, so this is a draft choice.",
  "Archways straddle the trail on six different legs with the measured gap (0.09 off centre) containing the corridor; the pivot sits on the centreline.",
  "Colonnades: eight in flanking pairs 11.5 studs from the centreline, six scattered in the courts.",
  "A server ray is assumed to start above the walls the way a stilt walker's would; whether 7 stud walls hide a player from its head is untested (the bible leaves the ray start open)."
 ],
